title: 'statement gossip: route the v2 propagation plan through the per-peer outbox'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, statements chosen by the propagation plan now
    go through the same per-peer outbox as v1 propagation: one chunk in flight per peer, the
    shared in-flight byte budget, a bounded queue and a retry after a failed store fetch.
    Planned statements bypass the peer's affinity filter and its sync watermark, and a
    transient statement travels through the outbox with its body. Nodes without the v2 DHT
    path enabled are unaffected.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: none
